Job Description:

As Userbase Manager you wil be responsible for:

The worldwide communication with and to our existing and new members;

In close collaboration with the Marketing Director, developing and executing the corporate strategy to recruit and retain new and existing members;

Managing regular research activity to understand member views and needs;

Managing production of regular statistics, analysis and reports on membership recruitment, growth and retention;

Initiate and follow-up of key-partnerships;

You define and follow-up our localization needs.

Skills:

You are in love with the online community and have a passion for a multicultural environment;

You are hands-on with 5+ years of consumer marketing experience on an international level in a young and dynamic environment;

You hold a Masters degree; an MBA is a plus;

You have the entrepreneurial skills and drive;

You have a broad experience and understanding of all facets of the marketing discipline including market research, segmentation, new product launch, and positioning;

You are multilingual.

Function

As a key member of the company, you will be responsible for content optimization with a view to strengthen organic search rankings and increasing traffic from Google, Yahoo, MSN and other search engines.

Skills and Experience

You have an excellent knowledge of SEO techniques; as well as link-building strategies for large database-driven sites;

You are good with words and understand search consumer behavior;

You grasp international cultural and language differences and are able to develop localized SEO marketing strategies;

You have strong problem-solving skills and an ability to identify new SEO solutions;

You hold a Masters degree, an MBA is a plus;

You understand HTML;

You are willing to travel;

You are very analytic, learn continuously and have an always-on mentality.

Function

We’re more than a normal website – we’re a social community platform with a unified mission to create unexpected ways of online advertising that change brand perception. We’re growing rapidly and have a variety of European and national accounts. We’re looking for someone with experience in selling of online media campaigns for multiple clients that goes beyond the banner. Strong interest and an in-depth understanding of the (digital) media landscape, including emerging media and social networking, dedication and the willingness to learn are a must.

You will drive online advertising revenues using integrated branding products of Netlog for Italy;

You will liaise with new strategic and revenue generating partners;

You will translate client marketing and advertising objectives into successful digital media strategies;

You will look beyond digital in order to develop the best possible campaign and results for our customers.

Skills and Experience

You hold a masters degree;

You speak fluently Italian and English, one of the following is a plus: French, German or Spanish;

You have a proven experience in a similar position (at least 3 years);

Personal Profile

You are a true communicator and negotiator;

You are result-driven, enthusiastic and highly demanding;

You have excellent commercial business skills;

You respect deadlines, and you are able to set the right priorities;

You are a team player and you enjoy working in various and dynamic teams;

You can cope with pressure and tight deadlines;

You are willing to travel.

Function

Working from our Belgian head office in Ghent:

You will drive online advertising revenues through making local sales houses successful and positioning Netlog’s integrated branding products in the DACH market;

You will liaise with new strategic and revenue generating partners;

You will translate client marketing and advertising objectives into successful digital media strategies;

You will look beyond digital in order to develop the best possible campaign and results for our customers.

Skills and Experience

You hold a masters degree;

You speak German and English fluent;

You have a first working experience (at one - two years);

You have a strong interest in the (digital) media landscape, including emerging media and social networking;

You are a true communicator and negotiator;

You are result-driven, enthusiastic and highly demanding;

You are a team player and you enjoy working in various and dynamic teams;

You are willing to travel approx 1/3 of your time.

Job Description:

You will be responsible for the coordination of activities and projects to develop and sustain relationships with Netlog members, including :

Preparation and reporting of meetings and presentations concerning Community;

Analysis of incoming reports/statistics/survey results about Netlog or competitors;

Gain and share insights in the Netlog community, supported by research and statistics;

Advise the Community Director on site related aspects, based on those insights;

Design, coordinate and evaluate localised projects to develop and sustain relationships with Netlog members;

Special assignments.

Skills and Experience:

You have:

A university degree;

A good understanding of Internet industry;

An excellent knowledge of English, Dutch and French;

A good knowledge of Office or iWork;

An experience in analysis, statistics and presentations.

Personal Profile:

You are:

A multi-tasking personality; organizational talent, stress proofed;

An outstanding project manager;

Highly flexible, discrete and reliable.

