description:
About the Company
We are ticketscript - the European market leader in digital self-ticketing. Whether it’s massive dance events, festivals, gigs, outdoor cinemas, fairs, theater shows, exhibitions, comedy nights, or award ceremonies - we do them all! We believe in empowering our customers. Their success is our success. So far over 50,000 events have worked with us - and this is only the beginning. We have offices in London, Amsterdam, Antwerp, Berlin and Barcelona and are rapidly expanding across Europe.

The role
The person we are looking for has a deep mix of marketing, communications, branding and online media strategy experience as well as management experience. The successful candidate has a dynamic personality to work with diverse and global stakeholders.
He/she is required to join and lead a dynamic marketing team that’s responsible for the creation and delivery of marketing campaigns across all customer touchpoints and all communication platforms. Our Marketing Managers are based in London, Amsterdam, Berlin and Barcelona. You will report to the CMO.

Whether we are part of ADE (Amsterdam Dance Event), relaunching our brand, liaising with journalists or providing marketing support for our clients - this is an incredible opportunity to make a real difference in an exciting, fast-paced entrepreneurial company.

Responsibilities
- Oversee brand identity globally across all channels and guards brand identity in terms of tone-of-voice, branding and visual identity;
- Manage a team of Marketing Managers and ensure that they have the context to deliver amazing campaigns to achieve our goal of the being the most successful digital self-ticketing solution - online and offline;
- Expand market positions;
- Control and responsible for the marketing budget;
- Identification of marketing opportunities and development of action planning activities;
- Management of daily marketing operations to achieve business objectives;
- Lead and support recruitment, career development, training and succession planning

requirements:
